  <!-- ABOUT -->
  <section id="about">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="label rv">Who we are</p>
      <h2 class="rv">A school small enough that no child is a stranger.</h2>
      <p class="intro rv">Emmanuel began as a prayer meeting in 2001. Two years later, in August 2003, the school opened its doors. It is still what those parents started: a school that belongs to families rather than to a chain, run by the Leicestershire Christian Education Trust.</p>
      <div class="three">
        <div class="rv">
          <h3>Christ at the centre</h3>
          <p>Not an assembly bolted onto an ordinary school day. What we believe about God shapes how we teach history, science, art and everything else &mdash; and how we speak to a child having a difficult morning.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rv">
          <h3>Small on purpose</h3>
          <p>Seven classes, and room for seventy-five children in the whole school. Every member of staff knows every child by name, and most will have taught them. Nobody drifts through unnoticed here.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rv">
          <h3>Alongside parents</h3>
          <p>We hold that raising children is entrusted to parents, not to schools. Our job is to support that work with skill and care, not to take it over.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

