  <!-- CURRICULUM -->
  <section id="learning">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="label rv">What your child would learn</p>
      <h2 class="rv">A full curriculum, taught by people who believe Christ holds it together.</h2>
      <p class="intro rv">Pupils here sit the same GCSEs as anywhere else and are taught the same subjects. What differs is the account we give of them. Our framework, <em>Christ in All Things</em>, takes its name from Colossians 1:17 &mdash; that in him all things hold together. In practice that means a science lesson is a science lesson, taught well, by someone who thinks the order they are studying was put there.</p>
      <div class="cards">
        <a class="card rv" href="/lower/">
          <span class="yrs">Willow &middot; Hazel</span>
          <h3>Lower School</h3>
          <p>Reception to Year 4. Reading, writing and number secured early, with the wider curriculum taught through topics across mixed-age classes.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="card rv" href="/middle/">
          <span class="yrs">Oak &middot; Maple</span>
          <h3>Middle School</h3>
          <p>Years 5 to 8. The move from one teacher to many, with specialist subject teaching alongside the pastoral care of a small class.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="card rv" href="/upper/">
          <span class="yrs">Birch &middot; Ash &middot; Cedar</span>
          <h3>Upper School &amp; GCSE</h3>
          <p>Years 9 to 11. GCSE courses with AQA and Eduqas, taught in groups small enough that no pupil can hide at the back.</p>
        </a>
      </div>
